.TH BACKUP_DIR 1 "May 4, 2025" "backup_dir" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
backup_dir \- Perform full or incremental backups with MD5 verification
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B backup_dir
.I src dest
.RB [ \-\-type
.IR {full|incr} ]
.RB [ \-\-timestamp
.IR timestamp_file ]
.RB [ \-\-log
.IR log_file
|
.BR \-l
.IR log_file ]
.RB [ \-\-verbose
|
.BR \-v ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B backup_dir
script performs full or incremental backups from a source directory
.I src
to a destination directory
.I dest
on Unix-like systems. It supports MD5 checksum verification, metadata preservation (permissions, timestamps, ownership), symbolic link handling, and ignore patterns via a
.I .backup_ignore
file. The destination directory must exist. The script prevents concurrent runs for the same source directory using a lock file.
.PP
In
.I full
mode, all non-ignored files are copied, overwriting files with different MD5 checksums, and extra files in the destination are deleted. In
.I incr
mode, only files with modification times newer than the timestamp file's modification time are copied (except symbolic links, which are always included unless ignored), and no files are deleted. Hidden files are included unless ignored.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI src
Source directory to back up (required).
.TP
.BI dest
Destination directory (required, must exist).
.TP
.BR \-\-type " {" full | incr }
Backup type: \fIfull\fR (default) or \fIincr\fR (incremental).
.TP
.BI \-\-timestamp " timestamp_file"
Path to timestamp file. Required for \fIincr\fR mode; optional for \fIfull\fR mode. Updated to backup start time after successful backup.
.TP
.BR \-\-log " log_file" " | " \-l " log_file"
Write logs to \fIlog_file\fR instead of stdout.
.TP
.BR \-\-verbose " | " \-v
Enable detailed logging, including all file operations and progress.
.SH .backup_ignore FILE
The
.I .backup_ignore
file in the source directory specifies files and directories to exclude, using
.I .gitignore
-like syntax:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Exact paths (e.g., \fIfile.txt\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Directories (e.g., \fIdir/\fR or \fIdir\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Wildcards (e.g., \fI*.txt\fR, \fIlogs/*\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Comments (lines starting with \fI#\fR)
.IP \(bu 2
Blank lines
.RE
.PP
Example:
.PP
.RS
.nf
*.log
temp/
# Ignore build outputs
build/*
.fi
.RE
.PP
Ignored files are not copied, deleted, or compared. Complex
.I .gitignore
features (e.g., negated patterns like \fI!file.txt\fR) are not supported.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Full backup with verbose logging:
.B backup_dir /src /dest \-\-type full \-\-log backup.log \-\-verbose
.TP
Incremental backup:
.B backup_dir /src /dest \-\-type incr \-\-timestamp /path/to/timestamp.txt
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful backup.
.TP
.B 1
Error (e.g., missing directories, invalid arguments, running instance for same source).
.SH NOTES
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Incremental mode uses file modification time (\fImtime\fR) for selection, except for symbolic links, which are always included unless ignored.
.IP \(bu 2
Metadata preservation (e.g., ownership) may fail without sufficient permissions, logging a warning.
.IP \(bu 2
Hidden files (e.g., \fI.file\fR) are included unless ignored.
.IP \(bu 2
The timestamp file, if provided, is updated to the backup start time.
.IP \(bu 2
Instance locking uses a lock file in \fI/tmp\fR based on a SHA-256 hash of the source directory path, preventing concurrent runs for the same source.
.RE
.SH BUGS
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Ownership preservation may fail without root privileges, logging a warning.
.IP \(bu 2
The
.I .backup_ignore
file does not support complex
.I .gitignore
features like negated patterns.
.RE
